=== SUMMARY: P2 shared-surfaces/0064 AreaChartWrapper ===
Native WinUI 3 parity port of web/src/components/charts/AreaChartWrapper.tsx -- a pure presentational,
chrome-free multi-series area-chart wrapper.

Files (the surface; AreaChartWrapper.*):
  - apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/shared-surfaces/AreaChartWrapper.Model.cs   (WinUI-free: model /
    projection / display / registration / diagnostics; Compile-linked into the headless test host).
  - apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/shared-surfaces/AreaChartWrapper.cs         (the bare WinUI view).
Test:
  - apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/SharedSurfaces/AreaChartWrapperTests.cs (50 headless cases).

Composition / parity:
  - Reuses the shared TsAreaChart cartesian primitive (the atomic chart in components/charts, P2
    component-library bundle) -- no direct recharts; the surface maps the web props onto it.
  - Web SeriesConfig {key,label,color}: key -> the row value lookup; label -> the series name / tooltip;
    the web hex `color` -> the W1 tokenized chart palette via ColorIndex (defaulting to the series'
    ordinal position) or a semantic ChartRole. Never hard-coded hex (the codebase chart contract).
  - X is plotted on an ordinal domain; the web xFormatter(row[xKey]) is applied to build each point's
    display label, surfaced as the native cartesian tooltip header (the accepted native convention the
    sibling SocChart / MonthlyCostChart document). The web yFormatter maps to per-series Unit / Decimals.
  - Web `height` (default 300) passes through; a non-positive / non-finite value falls back to 300. The
    web `className` styling hook has no native analog (documented; omitted).

States rendered (every state is a visible surface -- never a blank box):
  - Loading  : chart skeleton (TsChartSkeleton; suppresses its shimmer under OS reduce-motion).
  - Error    : QueryError equivalent (TsQueryError) with a Retry affordance (RetryRequested event).
  - Empty    : friendly empty surface (TsEmptyState) when there are no rows or no series.
  - Ready    : the multi-series area chart (the web fall-through render).
  - Stale    : the chart plus a warning freshness chip.
  - Offline  : the cached chart plus a danger freshness chip.
  Ready + Empty are the genuine web states; loading / error / stale / offline are the standard native
  async chrome the consuming surface drives around the presentational web component (the SocChart
  precedent) -- documented here, not silent drift.

i18n (P1/S10 facade; the web source is anonymous and owns no keys -- these are the native chrome keys,
reusing existing catalog entries): chart.noData, common.loading, common.retry, common.offline,
error.loadFailed, error.network.message (+ common.stale fallback "Stale" per the committed AchievementBadge
convention). No English literals in the view.

Accessibility: per-state Narrator name on the surface root; the chart figure carries the joined series
labels; the stale / offline chips carry names; the chart has no animation, so reduced-motion is honoured by
construction (only the loading skeleton pulses, and it suppresses its own shimmer under reduce-motion).

Telemetry: emits view.opened slug=AreaChartWrapper once on first show, via AreaChartWrapperDiagnostics
(PII-safe; never logs a data value, series label or row count -- asserted by a test).

Tests: 50 AreaChartWrapper headless cases (branch projection + precedence, the draw gate, the per-series
area mapping incl. ordinal X / row value on Y / missing-value-as-zero / x-label, positional + explicit
colour slots, role / unit / decimals, height passthrough + fallback, resolved chrome labels, freshness
chip, null-safety, per-state accessible names, and PII-safe diagnostics) -- all green. Full headless suite:
19433 / 19433 passed (TeslaSync.App.Tests.dll).

Meaningful placeholder scan (the gate's -Path .../AreaChartWrapper targets flat AreaChartWrapper.* files,
so it scans vacuously like every sibling flat-file surface; a per-file scan of the shipped files reports
PLACEHOLDER_COUNT=0 for AreaChartWrapper.Model.cs, AreaChartWrapper.cs and AreaChartWrapperTests.cs).

